# Katrin cable car valley station (Bad Ischl, opened 1959), back layer, no k:
# a 1950s concrete-and-glass hall i/m with a glass front s/h (m mullions),
# a door with b glass, and the boarding opening
# (m/d) with one small red cabin R (r lit edge, h/s windows, i roof) on its
# hanger. A canopy slab m/d at rows 20..23 runs behind the oneway_wood
# canopy tile (the tile is the surface; the art has no light lip there),
# carried by a post at its right end. Above it the drive house with a
# monopitch roof (m line, d underside: no ledge) and a ribbon window, and
# the exposed bull wheel (d rim, m spokes, i hub) with the two cable
# strands rising to the upper right (1 px d) out of the frame.
# Placement: 96x80, origin 48,80; place at col 35, row 14, dx 8 (x 0 = col
# 33, bottom on the street top): the canopy tile row 11 (64 px up) at cols
# 34..38 covers sprite rows 16..31 over x 16..95.
# Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway script; the grid is the source.
sprite = katrin_talstation
size   = 96x80
origin = 48,80
anim   = idle frames=1
